<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Stable ids for the chart's own accessibility actions.

  An `AccessibilityActionCompat` needs an id that is unique on the node and stable across processes,
  and the platform's guidance is to declare it as a resource rather than to pick an integer: the
  framework's own action ids are bit flags in a low range and nothing stops a hand-picked constant
  from colliding with one a future release adds.

  One per `ChartActionKind`. A kind added without an id here fails `VegaAccessibilityHelper`'s
  exhaustive `when`, which is the point of spelling them out rather than deriving from `ordinal`.
-->
<resources>
  <item name="aster_vega_action_zoom_in" type="id" />
  <item name="aster_vega_action_zoom_out" type="id" />
  <item name="aster_vega_action_reset_zoom" type="id" />
  <item name="aster_vega_action_reset_domains" type="id" />
  <!--
    The two directions of an **adjustable axis**, which is not a `ChartActionKind`: adjusting an
    axis is the increment and decrement of one element, not an action on the chart.

    Declared rather than reusing `ACTION_SCROLL_FORWARD`/`BACKWARD` on their own, because those are
    what the *element* offers and these are what names them in the recorded surface — without an id
    here the seam has no marker on the one host that owns the whole thing internally, and a row with
    no marker is a row that cannot fail. `VegaAccessibilityHelper` still adds the standard scroll
    actions, which is what TalkBack maps a swipe onto; these sit beside them.
  -->
  <item name="aster_vega_action_narrow_axis" type="id" />
  <item name="aster_vega_action_widen_axis" type="id" />
</resources>
